Negative control for the StringsRenderer facet-write fix (FE-3031, operator
sign-off 2026-09-09, "Authorise the one-line client-vue fix").

Assertion it attacks: the WIRE, not the model — after driving the status tile
then the category tile, `translateQuery(schema, model())` must produce
`filter[status.code|in]` carrying `"invoice_unpaid,invoice_overdue"` and
`filter[category.slug|in]` carrying `"recurrent"`. A prior version of this
patch attacked "the model carries the driven values" instead; that assertion
is too weak — the model carried *something* even under the wrong-path defect
this story's earlier cycle shipped (a nested `{status:{code:{in:[...]}}}}`),
so it could pass while the request the API actually receives stayed empty.
Grading the model rather than the wire is exactly the failure mode this
story's verifier named: "The mutant, the proof, and every green gate all
graded the model rather than the wire, which is precisely why this shipped
believing it worked."

PROVING ASSERTION EXISTS YET: NO. No committed test in
`packages/client-vue/src/**/__tests__/` or
`playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/__tests__/` yet drives a facet tile
and reads the WIRE (via `translateQuery`) back (that gate is the prover's,
named in this story's "Not yours" list — "a gate mounting the invoices bar
that asserts the wire"). The assertion named above lives today only in the
developer's own ephemeral driving-proof script used to prove this fix works
(`mountFilters` from `packages/client-vue/src/components/form/renderers/__tests__/filter.harness.ts`,
driven against the real, shipped `invoices.schemas.ts` declaration — imported
directly by absolute path from the scratch script, not transcribed, because
the script is never committed and carries no lint exposure). When the prover
lands the permanent gate, this patch attacks its facet-write-reaches-the-wire
assertion the same way; until then it is proven red against the developer's
own script, as recorded below.

Mutation: restores the no-op `handleChange: () => {}` — the whole-selection
write `onInput` hands off is swallowed entirely, so neither facet's click
ever reaches the criteria model, and `translateQuery` emits nothing for
either column.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

